<hr>
<h2>Appendix: Complete Feature List</h2>
<h3>Languages</h3>
<ul>
<li>English, Filipino, and Bisaya (Cebuano).</li>
<li>All six directions: English to Filipino, English to Bisaya, Filipino to English, Filipino to Bisaya, Bisaya to English, Bisaya to Filipino.</li>
<li>Explicit language selection at startup: both From and To show "Select language" and have no default.</li>
<li>Record, Translate, and Swap are disabled until both languages are chosen.</li>
<li>Swap button exchanges From and To and moves the translation to the input box.</li>
<li>Auto-detect was removed so the app cannot guess the wrong language and transcribe Bisaya speech as English.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Voice Input and Transcription</h3>
<ul>
<li>Record/Stop microphone button.</li>
<li>English and Filipino use the browser's Web Speech API.</li>
<li>Bisaya uses an online Cebuano speech recognition service: the SapinSapin halohalo demo on Hugging Face, using the <code>whisper-small-pld-ceb</code> model.</li>
<li>The app records the Bisaya audio, uploads it, waits for the transcription, and places the text in the left box.</li>
<li>Status messages: "Listening… speak Bisaya," "Uploading your Bisaya voice…," and "Transcribing Bisaya… the first run can take a few minutes."</li>
<li>Three-minute timeout and clear error messages if the online service is unreachable.</li>
<li>MediaRecorder captures the audio so it can be downloaded.</li>
<li>Auto translate after recording, or while recording for English and Filipino.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Translation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Free online translation: MyMemory with a backup online service; bad results are detected and retried.</li>
<li>Long text is split into smaller parts before translation.</li>
<li>Built-in offline phrasebook for common expressions when there is no internet.</li>
<li>Personal corrections saved in the browser and reused first for the same text.</li>
<li>Optional developer-only offline AI translation model (NLLB) via Transformers.js; needs a large model download.</li>
<li>Translation cache for repeated text.</li>
<li>Same-language selections return the same text.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Output and Actions</h3>
<ul>
<li>Editable translation box.</li>
<li>Copy translation and Clear all.</li>
<li>Save my correction.</li>
<li>Read aloud with a preferred female voice; if no female voice is installed, the pitch is raised.</li>
<li>Bisaya read-aloud falls back to a Filipino voice when no Cebuano voice is installed.</li>
<li>Stop while reading aloud.</li>
<li>Download as Text (.txt), Word (.doc), PDF (print window), or Subtitles (.srt).</li>
<li>Download the recorded audio (.webm, .ogg, or .m4a).</li>
<li>Saved list with language pair, date and time, favorites, read aloud, delete, favorites-only filter, download all, delete all, and clear corrections.</li>
<li>Keeps up to 200 saved translations.</li>
<li>Dark/light mode and A+/A− text size, both remembered in the browser.</li>
<li>Accessibility: labels for screen readers, roles, status announcements, and focus outlines.</li>
<li>Responsive layout for phones.</li>
<li>Privacy note: Bisaya recordings are sent to the public SapinSapin demo; English and Filipino use the browser's speech service, which may also be online.</li>
</ul>
</body>
